        "problem": "$\\int 3{x}^{2}{e}^{3{x}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=3{x}^{3}+1.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9{x}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=3{x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}{e}^{3{x}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3{x}^{3}+1}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3{x}^{3}+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
